1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,139
The outside pressure arrived as a call from the publisher's receptionist, on an occasion that nobody had marked in advance: the whole archive would be printed, or the contract would cease.

2
00:00:12,139 --> 00:00:18,028
“Whatever we do, the outcome is the same,” the director said.

3
00:00:18,028 --> 00:00:24,317
“We have barely three weeks, and the topic is not ours alone.”

4
00:00:24,317 --> 00:00:31,110
The hesitant answer was to renovate the old chapters temporarily and publish them afterward.

5
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:35,260
“Do it beforehand,” the receptionist said.

6
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:44,943
“A sudden blessing is still a blessing.” Somewhere in the building a printer started, and the hurry became real.

7
00:00:44,943 --> 00:00:54,092
The loyal reader, the shy volunteer, and the inspirational teacher were the only people who could check the whole series.

8
00:00:54,092 --> 00:00:59,506
“A worthless paragraph is worse than a missing one,” Maya wrote.

9
00:00:59,506 --> 00:01:04,610
“A miraculous figure is usually a deficient one.”

10
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:11,374
The instinctive reaction of the group was to glance at the mode of the distribution and stop there.

11
00:01:11,374 --> 00:01:17,587
“A holy number and a momentary one look alike on a page,” the auditor said.

12
00:01:17,587 --> 00:01:24,846
“The pronoun in the sentence tells you who is responsible, and the verb tells you when.”

13
00:01:24,846 --> 00:01:30,675
The thirst for a clean ending was strong, and the ending would not be clean.

14
00:01:30,675 --> 00:01:37,259
“A virtuous account and a sacrificial one are different kinds of writing,” Lin said.

15
00:01:37,259 --> 00:01:42,628
“One costs money; the other costs somebody.”

16
00:01:42,628 --> 00:01:56,160
The pressure produced a decision that was neither heroic nor worthless: an hourly check for three weeks, a temporary revision, and a promise that the next edition would carry everything.

17
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:04,469
Whenever the group published one page, the editor asked for another, and the work never once became easy.

18
00:02:04,469 --> 00:02:10,633
Although we believe in the build, the effect of everything else is too hard to measure.

19
00:02:10,633 --> 00:02:16,172
He himself shall feel the pressure, and she should, too.

20
00:02:16,172 --> 00:02:25,590
Therefore we shall try to bring the whole record to the press, and the important thing is the life of the reader rather than the life of the author.

21
00:02:25,590 --> 00:02:33,063
It was upon this page that the two friends agreed, and it is to this page that the archive returns.

22
00:02:33,063 --> 00:02:40,487
The hard part is not the printing; it is the choosing, and everything else is a matter of time.

23
00:02:40,487 --> 00:02:58,544
We want to say, before anything else, that we have tried ever since: somehow, anywhere, sometime, we scarcely had a saying in it, and no guarantee whatsoever, because the deadline was not ours to move.

24
00:02:58,544 --> 00:03:07,823
There was no bridge chapter left to write, and that, too, was a fact they had to publish.
